hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18465","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Muhammad ibn Hatib who said: I reached for a pot belonging to my mother and my hand burned, so my mother took me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he wiped my hand, and I do not know what he said, I was too young for that, so I asked my mother and she said: He said: Remove the harm, Lord of the people, and heal, You are the Healer, there is no healing but Your healing."
"18466","Aswad ibn Amir and Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas both said: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Muhammad ibn Hatib who said: I drew near to a pot of ours and my hand burned, Ibrahim said: Or he said: It swelled, so my mother took me to a man, and he spoke words I do not know what they were and blew, so I asked my mother during the caliphate of Uthman who the man was, and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"18467","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abi Malik al-Ashjai who said: I was sitting with Muhammad ibn Hatib, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have seen a land with palm trees, so go out, so Hatib and Jafar went out by sea toward al-Najashi, and I was born in that ship."
"18468","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abu Balj narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Hatib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What distinguishes the lawful from the unlawful is the voice and the beating of the tambourine."
"18469","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abi Balj who said: I said to Muhammad ibn Hatib: I married two women with no tambourine beaten for me, he said: Evil is what you did, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What distinguishes the lawful from the unlawful is the voice, meaning the beating of the tambourine."
"18470","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Muhammad ibn Hatib who said: The pot fell on my hand and my hand burned, so my father took me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he spat on it and said: Remove the harm, Lord of the people, and I think he said: And heal him, You are the Healer."
